    "details": "Wasmtime development team reports:\n\n> - wasi-sockets: UDP connect only required the address to be permitted\n>   for sending or receiving, allowing guests to send datagrams to\n>   addresses denied for UdpSend.\n> - Cross-engine type confusion with host-created\n>   struct-types-with-supertypes has been fixed.\n> - Panic with typed functions with i31 or nullref arguments has been\n>   fixed.\n> - Unchecked memory usage in transferring borrowed resources between\n>   components has been fixed.\n> - Fixed a possibility of content-length being invalid or not matching\n>   body length in wasi-http p2.\n",
    "id": "FreeBSD-2026-0583",
